ONNX Runtime (pinned ORT_VERSION): send unsorted TopK requests whose SafeSmallKTopK
shared memory would exceed the workgroup LDS limit to RadixTopK, instead of a
launch that cannot run. Applies after topk-radix-tiebreak-nondeterministic.patch.

WHY
---
topk-radix-tiebreak-nondeterministic.patch routes every request that reaches the
`K <= BT * 16 || 0 == sorted` branch of TopKImpl (BT = 256) to SafeSmallKTopK. That
kernel takes dynamic shared memory of

    smem_bytes = 256 * (sizeof(T) + sizeof(int64_t)) + K * sizeof(int64_t)

The K term exists because the kernel keeps the K indices it has already selected in
shared memory. For sorted output the branch is only reached with K <= 4096, so
smem_bytes is at most 256 * 16 + 8 * 4096 = 36864 bytes and always fits. For unsorted
output the `0 == sorted` clause admits any K up to the axis length, and smem_bytes
passes the 64 KiB LDS limit of a gfx803 workgroup at

    K > 7808 for float   (256 * 12 + 8 * K > 65536)
    K > 7872 for fp16    (256 * 10 + 8 * K > 65536)
    K > 7680 for double  (256 * 16 + 8 * K > 65536)

A launch that asks for more LDS than the device has runs no block, and TopKImpl does
not check the launch status, so the op can return success with output buffers that
were never written. Without the topk-radix patch the same requests go to RadixTopK,
which handles them.

RadixTopK serves this case. Its shared memory is a fixed 256 * sizeof(uint32_t) plus
a static BlockScan/BlockReduce/BlockRadixSort union, independent of K. With
`0 == sorted` the dispatch condition `BT * 2 >= K || 0 == sorted` selects the
RadixTopK<CudaT, BT, 2> instantiation for every K, and that instantiation never runs
the final BlockRadixSort step (guarded by `1 == sorted`), so K is not limited by KPT.
For exactly tied candidates at the K-th value, RadixTopK can still pick a different
winner from run to run (the defect SafeSmallKTopK was added for); that remains possible
only for unsorted requests with K above the bound.

SafeSmallKTopK is also quadratic in K per block (every candidate scans the K selected
indices on every pass), so a large unsorted K is much cheaper through RadixTopK than
through a kernel that would fit.

WHAT
----
Compare smem_bytes with a 64 KiB bound before launching SafeSmallKTopK. Above it, launch
RadixTopK<CudaT, BT, 2> with the same arguments the CUDA path uses. Only that
instantiation can be reached on ROCm (the bound is exceeded only when sorted == 0), so
the other RadixTopK instantiations stay out of the ROCm build, which keeps this file's
compile time as it is. The non-ROCm path is untouched.

VERIFICATION (RX 590, gfx803, image built with this patch):
tools/correctness-suite/pytorch/ort_topk_smem_bound_check.py runs TopK with sorted = 0 at K above the bound (7808 for
float, 7872 for fp16) for float and fp16, largest 0 and 1, against a numpy reference: 20 of 20 cases pass. Without the
patch the ROCm EP raises hipErrorInvalidValue for those requests (the launch asks for more than 64 KiB of LDS), so TopK
with sorted = 0 is unusable above the bound. The cases just below the bound (--include-below) go through the quadratic
SafeSmallKTopK and were not run.

diff --git a/onnxruntime/core/providers/cuda/math/topk_impl.cuh b/onnxruntime/core/providers/cuda/math/topk_impl.cuh
index 667576f..01b5fbb 100644
--- a/onnxruntime/core/providers/cuda/math/topk_impl.cuh
+++ b/onnxruntime/core/providers/cuda/math/topk_impl.cuh
@@ -560,10 +560,21 @@ Status TopKImpl(const CudaKernel* kernel, bool use_deterministic_compute,
 
 #ifdef USE_ROCM
     // SAFE_SMALL_K_TOPK_PATCH: see the kernel's own comment above for why.
+    // SAFE_SMALL_K_SMEM_BOUND: the kernel's dynamic shared memory grows with K, and a launch that asks for more
+    // than the workgroup's 64 KiB of LDS runs no block at all. Only unsorted output can get there (with sorted
+    // output this branch has K <= BT * 16, which always fits), and RadixTopK serves unsorted output for any K.
+    constexpr size_t kSafeSmallKMaxSmemBytes = 64 * 1024;
     size_t smem_bytes = GridDim::maxThreadsPerBlock * (sizeof(CudaT) + sizeof(int64_t)) + K * sizeof(int64_t);
-    SafeSmallKTopK<CudaT><<<N, GridDim::maxThreadsPerBlock, smem_bytes, stream>>>(
-        input_x_ptr, output_v_ptr, output_i, elem_nums, size, axis, K, largest, sorted, dimension,
-        NumericLimits<CudaT>::Lowest(), NumericLimits<CudaT>::Max());
+    if (smem_bytes <= kSafeSmallKMaxSmemBytes) {
+      SafeSmallKTopK<CudaT><<<N, GridDim::maxThreadsPerBlock, smem_bytes, stream>>>(
+          input_x_ptr, output_v_ptr, output_i, elem_nums, size, axis, K, largest, sorted, dimension,
+          NumericLimits<CudaT>::Lowest(), NumericLimits<CudaT>::Max());
+    } else {
+      auto XPT = static_cast<int64_t>(ceil(static_cast<double>(dimension) / GridDim::maxThreadsPerBlock));
+      RadixTopK<CudaT, BT, 2><<<N, BT, 256 * sizeof(uint32_t), stream>>>(
+          input_x_ptr, output_v_ptr, output_i, elem_nums, size, axis, K, largest, sorted, dimension, XPT,
+          NumericLimits<CudaT>::Lowest(), NumericLimits<CudaT>::Max());
+    }
 #else
     auto XPT = static_cast<int64_t>(ceil(static_cast<double>(dimension) / GridDim::maxThreadsPerBlock));
     if (BT * 2 >= K || 0 == sorted) {
